# WARP-8: the FX sequence (docs/FX-SEQUENCE.md), drawn and played as the throws' sequence: sixteen squares, a black
# key picks a lane, a white key is a step with an amount (a tap: the lane's last, or off; held: knob 1; held and a
# later key: the amount on every step between). The amounts are the effects' own: FX II's ALL here. A fifth row on Scenes, and its mute
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
expect page Steps
turn ALGO -1
wait 40
expect trk 9
expect page Steps
expect lanes 0
# FX II's ALL (the sixth black key): steps 13 to 16
tapkey b5
wait 40
said LANE
# step 13 held, step 16 pressed: the amount on 13 to 16, as a throw is made longer
key w12 down
wait 100
key w15 down
wait 60
key w15 up
key w12 up
wait 40
said LENGTH
expect lanes 1
# step 16 louder: held, knob 1
key w15 down
wait 100
turn K1 20
wait 500
said AMOUNT
key w15 up
wait 40
expect lanes 1
shot fxseq.png
# another lane: FX I's first knob on step 1; a tap again takes it off, and the lane goes
tapkey b1
tapkey w0
wait 40
expect lanes 2
tapkey w0
wait 40
expect lanes 1
# it plays with the beat: a kick on the kit, a bar and a half
turn ALGO 1
wait 40
expect trk 1
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tap PLAY
wait 3000
tap PLAY
# Scenes: the fifth row, its mute on the fifth black key
tap HOME
turn SELECT 1
wait 40
expect page Scenes
shot fxseq_scenes.png
tapkey b4
wait 40
expect mute 256
tapkey b4
wait 40
expect mute 0
# EDIT has nothing for the FX sequence: back to the instrument
press HOME
turn ALGO -1
release HOME
wait 40
expect trk 9
tap EDIT
wait 40
expect trk 1
